\description{
Returns a single NBA draft pick. Defaults to the most recent NBA
season's #1 overall pick. For a full draft, use \code{\link[=espn_nba_draft]{espn_nba_draft()}}.

Returns one row per round of the NBA draft (typically 2 rounds:
1st with 30 picks, 2nd with ~28 picks).

Returns one row per drafted athlete in a given NBA draft year.

Returns the current status of one NBA draft year (round, state,
description). Live during the draft; static afterward.

Returns a single-row tibble with top-level draft-year metadata: year,
number of rounds, display name, plus \verb{$ref}s for the deeper sub-resources
(status, athletes, rounds) already wrapped by \code{\link[=espn_nba_draft_status]{espn_nba_draft_status()}},
\code{\link[=espn_nba_draft_athletes]{espn_nba_draft_athletes()}}, and \code{\link[=espn_nba_draft_rounds]{espn_nba_draft_rounds()}}.

Returns rich single-row detail for one drafted athlete in one NBA
draft year: name, height, weight, position, pick (overall/round/team),
and a \verb{$ref} to the athlete's core-v2 profile. Use
\code{\link[=espn_nba_draft_athletes]{espn_nba_draft_athletes()}} to enumerate draftees for a year.
}
\details{
\strong{Get ESPN NBA Draft Pick Detail}

\strong{Get ESPN NBA Draft Rounds Summary}

\strong{Get ESPN NBA Draft Athletes Index}

\strong{Get ESPN NBA Draft Status}

Calls the ESPN core-v2 endpoint
\verb{https://sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/basketball/leagues/nba/seasons/\{year\}/draft/rounds},
which returns each round of the draft with its picks inlined as \verb{picks: [...]}.
For historical seasons with no ESPN draft data the function returns an empty
tibble rather than erroring.
}
